## 5. Stakeholder Information Needs

Different stakeholder groups require different types of information from the assessment. The assessment should provide information appropriate to each stakeholder's role while maintaining a consistent current-state evidence base.

| Stakeholder Group | Primary Information Needs |
|---|---|
| Executive Leadership | Consolidated findings, significant risks and gaps, dependencies, unresolved questions, decision-readiness considerations |
| Clinical Leadership | Clinical workflow dependencies, device criticality, continuity considerations, information needs, operational impacts |
| Clinical Users | Workflow relationships, usability considerations, information availability, connectivity dependencies, known workarounds or constraints |
| Clinical Engineering / Biomedical Engineering | Device inventory, lifecycle position, maintenance dependencies, vendor support, device characteristics |
| IT Infrastructure / Networking | Connectivity relationships, network dependencies, monitoring, infrastructure boundaries, security dependencies |
| Integration / Interface Team | Interfaces, information flows, system relationships, ownership, monitoring, integration dependencies |
| Cybersecurity | Connectivity and exposure, lifecycle and support conditions, access, monitoring, security update considerations, cybersecurity dependencies |
| EHR / Clinical Systems Team | System relationships, information exchange, clinical workflow dependencies, integration considerations |
| Vendor / Manufacturer Representatives | Device capabilities, lifecycle information, support status, technical documentation, vendor-specific dependencies |
